==Russian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ru|изо-}}, {{l|ru|ис-}}

===Prefix===
{{head|ru|prefix}}

# [[out]] [[from]]
#: {{ru-ux|[[идти́]]|to go|inline=y}}
#: {{ru-ux|[[исходить|изойти́]]|to emanate, to originate, to come from|inline=y}}
# when added to a verb, it may form a verb with a sense of completeness, abundance or exhaustion
#: {{ru-ux|[[укра́сить]]|to decorate|inline=y}}
#: {{ru-ux|[[изукра́сить]]|lavishly decorate|inline=y}}
# when added to a verb, it may form a verb with a sense of destruction, ruined due to use
#: {{ru-ux|[[писа́ть]]|to write|inline=y}}
#: {{ru-ux|[[исписа́ть]]|write upon, cover with notes, write over|inline=y}}
# when added to nouns, specially when they have the suffix ье, it indicates location of an object
#: {{ru-ux|[[голова́]]|head|inline=y}}
#: {{ru-ux|[[изголо́вье]]|head of the bed|inline=y}}
# when added to adjectives for colours, an adverb is formed indicating nuance
#: {{ru-ux|[[жёлтый]]|yellow|inline=y}}
#: {{ru-ux|[[исжелта-]]|yellowish|inline=y}}
# when added to adjectives, it may form an adverb indicating spatial or temporal properties. Usually on archaic or highly formal style.
#: {{ru-ux|[[да́льний]]|far, distant|inline=y}}
#: {{ru-ux|[[и́здали]]|from afar|inline=y}}
# When added to adverbs, it can form an adverb with a sense of direction for an action
#: {{ru-ux|[[вну́тренний]]|interior, inner|inline=y}}
#: {{ru-ux|[[изнутри́]]|from inside|inline=y}}

